{# Canvas display settings — the "Zobrazení" check menu in the editor TOP bar
   (shared by the single-variant and the group editor). The switches are set
   once in a while, so they live behind one button.

   The element IDs are load-bearing: canvas_floating_toolbar
   (#highlight-editable-control + #caption-visible-control), canvas_container
   (#container-zones-control), canvas_snapping (#snap-enabled-control on
   connect) and canvas_rulers (#ruler-enabled-control) key off them. A
   Bootstrap dropdown keeps its menu in the DOM while closed, so those
   connect-time querySelector reads still find their switch.

   Look (Nocturne, prototype screen 21): every row is a menu item with a check
   mark — the checkbox itself is restyled into the mark (editor.css
   `.editor-display-menu`), it stays a real <input role="switch">.

   auto-close="outside": flipping one switch must not dismiss the menu — these
   are usually toggled in twos and threes. Both editor roots wrap the header,
   so the data-actions reach the same controllers as before. #}
<div class="dropdown ed-view">
    <button class="btn btn-ghost sm ed-view-btn" type="button" data-bs-toggle="dropdown"
            data-bs-auto-close="outside" aria-expanded="false" title="Co se zobrazuje na plátně">
        {{ icon('layers', 's16') }}<span class="ed-lbl">Zobrazení</span>
    </button>

    <div class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end editor-display-menu">
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="highlight-editable-control">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="highlight-editable-control" checked data-action="change->canvas-floating-toolbar#toggleHighlight">
            <span>Zobrazit editovatelné prvky</span>
        </label>
        {# Independent of the outline switch above: the two draw different halves of
           the same overlay, and a designer reviewing the composition usually wants
           the frames without the name tags covering the top of every element. #}
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="caption-visible-control" title="Jmenovky polí zobrazené v rohu každého editovatelného prvku">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="caption-visible-control" checked data-action="change->canvas-floating-toolbar#toggleCaptions">
            <span>Popisky vstupů pro klienta</span>
        </label>
        {# Chrome only — hiding the frames never touches the container DEFINITIONS
           (they keep reflowing the design and stay listed in the Kontejnery panel). #}
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="container-zones-control" title="Přerušované rámečky kontejnerů na plátně. Kontejnery zůstávají funkční, jen je nevidíte.">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="container-zones-control" checked data-action="change->canvas-container#toggleZones">
            <span>Rámečky kontejnerů</span>
        </label>
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="snap-enabled-control">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="snap-enabled-control" checked data-action="change->canvas-snapping#toggleSnapping">
            <span>Přichytávání k prvkům <span class="ed-vm-hint">⌘ = vypnout</span></span>
        </label>
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="ruler-enabled-control">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="ruler-enabled-control" checked data-action="change->canvas-rulers#toggle">
            <span>Pravítka a vodítka</span>
        </label>
        {# Chrome only (editor_chrome_controller): hides the movable mini-map
           panel; canvas_navigator_controller keeps drawing it underneath. #}
        <label class="ed-vm-row" for="navigator-visible-control">
            <input type="checkbox" role="switch" id="navigator-visible-control" checked data-action="change->editor-chrome#toggleNavigator">
            <span>Mini navigátor</span>
        </label>
    </div>
</div>
